§ It can have no more than 100 members. Husbands and wives count as
one member, even if they own separate shares of stock. In some instances,
family members count as one member.

@ All shareholders must agree to have the corporation formed as a subchapter
S corporation.

The primary disadvantages of a subchapter S corporation are restrictions
in qualifying, expenses involved with setting up and maintaining the
subchapter S status, and the fact that a subchapter S corporation is limited to
100 shareholders.*° If a subchapter S corporation wants to include more than
